  "details": "When you switch to some avatars (for example the Lightning McQueen one I made for me and my friends to use), upon switching to another avatar it persists client-side.\n\nExpected: When you change avatar it removes the model of the old one and successfully initializes the new one.\n\nResult: For everyone except the user changing avatar it successfully changes, however, for the user who changed avatars the original model stays and the new model loads in addition. Sometimes the newly loaded model is also not rigged.\n\nCurrent workaround: If you change avatar and it breaks in this manner, loading into a world fixes the bug and uses the avatar you changed to, thus going home and coming back to the world you were in fixes this.\nAttached images: Avatar before switching back, avatar after switching back (looking in mirror, no reflection), avatar after switching back (looking at self, two models visibly present).\n\nCurrent Version: 2021.2.1p2",
